<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  launchd job for the operator dashboard (scripts/run_dashboard.py; operator
  decision surface unit, 2026-08-03, launchd deploy broken follow up). Until
  this file existed there was no way to run the dashboard unattended at
  all: an operator had to start scripts/run_dashboard.py by hand, in a
  terminal, every time. See deploy/README.md for installation and the
  placeholder values below.

  Every /REPLACE/... value below is a placeholder. Fill them in for your
  own machine before loading this job; do not put a raw secret anywhere in
  this file (this script reads no credential and constructs no broker
  adapter at all, see agent/dashboard_server.py's own module docstring's
  "what this surface must never do").

  LOOPBACK ONLY, ALWAYS. The host flag is pinned to 127.0.0.1 explicitly,
  not left to its own (already 127.0.0.1) default: this surface has no
  authentication of its own and agent.dashboard_server.make_server refuses
  any other host outright, but a template should say so explicitly rather
  than relying on a default silently staying safe forever.

  THE SAME DATA DIR TREATMENT AS THE RECONCILIATION LOOP'S OWN PLIST. One
  data dir flag, not four separate individual path flags: see that plist's
  own top-of-file comment for why enumerating store paths individually is
  exactly the maintenance burden that crash looped the OTHER job in
  production. Point this job's data dir at the SAME directory as a real
  com.investmentagent.reconcile-loop job's own data dir: this script
  attaches a read/decide surface onto that SAME durable state (cost
  ledger, approval requests, opportunity tracker, audit log), not a
  second, independent copy of it. See scripts/run_dashboard.py's own
  module docstring.

  THE ACCOUNT ID FLAG IS OPTIONAL FOR THIS SCRIPT (unlike the reconciliation
  loop's own account id flag, which is required). Passing it here is still
  recommended for a real, single-account pilot: without it, GET
  /api/state's approvals.outstanding_earmarks_usd reports null with an
  unavailable-reason string instead of a real figure (see
  agent/dashboard_state.py's own module docstring). See this unit's own
  report for the fuller list of what this dashboard does NOT wire up yet
  (broker_account, broker_positions, day_trade_guard).

  CANONICAL DIRECTORY IS `data/`, NOT `state/`; see com.investmentagent.
  reconcile-loop.plist's own comment for why this template's example
  changed (runtime-recovery unit, 2026-08-13). Point this at the SAME
  absolute path you give that job's own data-dir flag.

  THE KEY ID, SECRET REF, AND SIGNING KEY SECRET REF FLAGS, ADDED
  (overnight hardening unit, 2026-08-13; DASHBOARD BROKER-STATE
  PROVENANCE finding). This template previously omitted these three flags
  entirely, even though scripts/run_dashboard.py has accepted them since
  Unit 16/17 (2026-08-12). For a deployment where config.json sets broker
  to "alpaca_paper" (not the "simulator" default), that omission is the
  most likely real cause of "settled cash, NLV, reserve, and investable
  cash all report unavailable": with neither flag supplied,
  agent.broker.selection.select_broker_adapter raises BrokerSelectionError
  inside scripts.run_dashboard._build_broker_state, which degrades (by
  design, never crashes) to broker_account=None. An installed copy of the
  OLD version of this template, silently missing these three flags, would
  reproduce exactly that symptom on every restart. Filling them in here
  (the SAME values as the reconcile-loop job's own key id, secret ref, and
  signing key secret ref flags; see scripts/install_launchagents.py, which
  renders both plists from the SAME parameters for exactly this reason)
  closes that gap. Harmless for the broker "simulator" default
  (scripts/run_dashboard.py's own docstring: unused and optional for that
  default).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.investmentagent.dashboard</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/REPLACE/WITH/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/investmentagent/scripts/run_dashboard.py</string>
        <string>--config</string>
        <string>/REPLACE/WITH/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/config.json</string>
        <string>--account-id</string>
        <string>REPLACE_WITH_ACCOUNT_ID</string>
        <string>--key-id</string>
        <string>REPLACE_WITH_ALPACA_PAPER_KEY_ID</string>
        <string>--secret-ref</string>
        <string>REPLACE_WITH_KEYCHAIN_SECRET_REF</string>
        <string>--signing-key-secret-ref</string>
        <string>REPLACE_WITH_SIGNING_KEY_SECRET_REF</string>
        <string>--data-dir</string>
        <string>/REPLACE/WITH/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/data</string>
        <string>--host</string>
        <string>127.0.0.1</string>
        <string>--port</string>
        <string>8765</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Start when the job is loaded, same reasoning as the reconciliation
         loop's own plist. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Restart on a non-zero exit only, same reasoning as the
         reconciliation loop's own plist: this process is meant to run
         forever (server.serve_forever()), so a non-zero exit means it
         crashed, not that it finished. -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>

    <!-- Same reasoning as the reconciliation loop's own plist: bounds a
         permanent failure (e.g. a config that no longer parses) to one
         relaunch attempt a minute rather than a tight crash loop. -->
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>

    <!-- Separate files, not one shared path, same reasoning as the
         reconciliation loop's own plist. Directory must exist and be
         writable before this job is loaded. -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/REPLACE/WITH/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/logs/dashboard.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/REPLACE/WITH/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/logs/dashboard.err.log</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
